# Build context excludes for the @peable.to/backend image (context = repo root).
#
# Use the **/ prefix so BuildKit matches NESTED directories too — a bare
# `node_modules` / `dist` only matches the top-level entry, leaving stale
# per-package copies in the context (and, for node_modules, a bloated/incorrect
# install layer). See ~/Oxy/AGENTS.md (.dockerignore rule).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.expo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/__tests__

.git
.github
docs
*.md
*.log
coverage
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local

# Exclude the heavy Expo frontend source from the backend build context, but
# KEEP its package.json: bun's frozen-lockfile install requires every workspace
# member's manifest to be present, otherwise the lockfile is treated as
# out-of-date and the install fails.
packages/frontend/*
!packages/frontend/package.json

# Same treatment for `@peable.to/pay`: the backend does not import it (it is the
# wallet-side money library), but its manifest has to be in the install context
# or `--frozen-lockfile` refuses the whole workspace. Its SOURCE is excluded for
# the same reason the frontend's is — it would otherwise be copied into every
# build context for nothing.
packages/pay/*
!packages/pay/package.json
